.TH V7AS 1 "August 2026" "V7 toolchain" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
v7as, v7as2 \- V7 PDP-11 assembler, pass 1 and pass 2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B v7as
[
.B \-
|
.B \-u
] [
.B \-o
objfile
] file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I v7as
assembles the concatenation of the named files.  It is the Seventh
Edition Unix assembler, translated from its original assembly sources
into C so it runs host-side as a cross-assembler.
.PP
The assembler is two passes.  Pass 1
.RB ( v7as ,
from
.IR as11.s .. as19.s )
builds the symbol table and assigns addresses; pass 2
.RB ( v7as2 ,
from
.IR as21.s .. as29.s )
emits the code and relocations and writes the object.
.I v7as
runs pass 1 and then itself executes
.B v7as2
(pass 2), locating it beside
.B v7as
or via the
.B AS2
environment variable.
.PP
If the optional argument
.B \-
(or its synonym
.BR \-u )
is used, all undefined symbols in the assembly are treated as global.
.PP
The output of the assembly is left on the file
.IR objfile ;
if that is omitted,
.B a.out
is used.  It is executable if no errors occurred during the assembly, and
if there were no unresolved external references.
.SH FILES
v7as2	pass 2 of the assembler (found beside v7as, or via $AS2)
.br
/tmp/atm[1-3]?	temporary
.br
a.out	object (magic 0407)
.SH "SEE ALSO"
v7ld(1),
nm(1),
adb(1),
a.out(5)
.br
.I "UNIX Assembler Manual"
by D. M. Ritchie
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
When an input file cannot be read, its name followed by a question mark is
typed and assembly ceases.  When syntactic or semantic errors occur, a
single-character diagnostic is typed out together with the line number and
the file name in which it occurred.  Errors in pass 1 cause cancellation of
pass 2.  The possible errors are:
.PP
.ta 3
)	Parentheses error
.br
]	Parentheses error
.br
<	String not terminated properly
.br
*	Indirection used illegally
.br
.li
\fB.\fR	Illegal assignment to `\fB.\fR'
.br
a	Error in address
.br
b	Branch instruction is odd or too remote
.br
e	Error in expression
.br
f	Error in local (`f' or `b') type symbol
.br
g	Garbage (unknown) character
.br
i	End of file inside an if
.br
m	Multiply defined symbol as label
.br
o	Word quantity assembled at odd address
.br
p	`\fB.\fR' different in pass 1 and 2
.br
r	Relocation error
.br
u	Undefined symbol
.br
x	Syntax error
.SH BUGS
Syntax errors can cause incorrect line numbers in following diagnostics.
